                "entry_id": "ae837a45-7ee5-3ccc-9128-6e45b8aa124c",
                "word": "pteridophyte",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "58a4d558-98ca-4196-8599-0cafc1b1b885",
                        "entry_id": "ae837a45-7ee5-3ccc-9128-6e45b8aa124c",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "pteridophytes"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e16cc281-2d8b-38ea-99c8-8b8d8fb05c88",
                        "entry_id": "ae837a45-7ee5-3ccc-9128-6e45b8aa124c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Any plant of the division Pteridophyta, of simple vascular plants that reproduce via spores rather than seeds and that alternate generations of diploid (sporophyte) and haploid (gametophyte or prothallus) forms, the diploid generally being larger and more conspicuous."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d2a5e195-27da-4b1a-8a07-c789f3c995bc",
                                "sense_id": "e16cc281-2d8b-38ea-99c8-8b8d8fb05c88",
                                "text": "Ferns, lycopods, and scouring rushes are all pteridophytes."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "72efb5d3-7247-486d-ba81-3e811d61c22d",
                                "sense_id": "e16cc281-2d8b-38ea-99c8-8b8d8fb05c88",
                                "text": "Most pteridophytes are homosporous, producing one type of spore that germinates to produce a potentially bisexual gametophyte."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "22ea7c05-7443-4577-aa3d-001a8a66d0ad",
                                "sense_id": "e16cc281-2d8b-38ea-99c8-8b8d8fb05c88",
                                "text": "1990, A. C. Jermy, Conservation of Ppteridophytes, K.U. Kramer, Klaus Kubitzki, P.S. Green, Pteridophytes and Gymnosperms, page 14,\nPteridophytes have evolved to fill almost every ecological niche but the greatest species diversity is clearly found in the tropical rainforest. The rapid disappearance of this biome throughout the world with many of their pteridophyte species yet undiscovered, let alone described, is of great concern."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d9f93fd3-68c1-47e5-9ece-839d53454978",
                                "sense_id": "e16cc281-2d8b-38ea-99c8-8b8d8fb05c88",
                                "text": "Pteridophytes are known from as far back as the Silurian, or some 380 million years ago. During the Silurian and the immediately succeeding Lower Devonian there were a considerable number of psilophytes of much simpler construction than any other known type of pteridophyte."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "1a36bab2-bf5f-498d-8af5-7c3467adebb9",
                        "source_entry_id": "ae837a45-7ee5-3ccc-9128-6e45b8aa124c",
                        "source_sense_id": "e16cc281-2d8b-38ea-99c8-8b8d8fb05c88",
                        "source_sense_description": "vascular plants that produce spores but not seeds",
                        "target_lang_word": "ptéridophyte",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "ptéridophyte",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8856a722-17a4-38e3-8dab-304119ff0a0e",
                                        "entry_id": "69b0aa19-c133-3c8f-8c82-f9649676d61c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Membre d'une division de trachéophytes comprenant des plantes cryptogames qui ont des vaisseaux conducteurs, et donc des racines, des tiges et des feuilles ou des frondes, mais pas encore de graines, de fruits ni de fleurs et forment des spores."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5d81d9fa-5a05-410b-9c38-031eb15c58ed",
                                                "sense_id": "8856a722-17a4-38e3-8dab-304119ff0a0e",
                                                "text": "Le développement des corylaies modifie la végétation bordière herbacée des abords du site avec la forte diminution des Apiaceae, Filipendula et Betula, et sur le site lui-même avec la baisse des Ptéridophytes."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3a4dbb5d-50a0-4459-9200-67090ae75c46",
                                                "sense_id": "8856a722-17a4-38e3-8dab-304119ff0a0e",
                                                "text": "Les grandes Ptéridophytes, caractéristiques du Primaire, ne se rencontrent actuellement que dans les forêts chaudes et humides de la zone équatoriale, où les saisons sont, en effet, peu marquées (fig. 96) ; nous pouvons donc affirmer que pendant le Primaire, la Terre tout entière avait un climat chaud et humide analogue à celui des forêts équatoriales du Brésil, de l’Inde ou de Java."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dfbdb674-cee5-42fa-8082-5c42a3a1909f",
                                                "sense_id": "8856a722-17a4-38e3-8dab-304119ff0a0e",
                                                "text": "Les grands Ptéridophytes disparaissent, et des Conifères rappelant les types actuels font leur apparition."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
